From: Stoicoci Mihaita <stoicocimihaita@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] q706f: select the Lenovo Wi-Fi board data with a calibration variant

*** DO NOT APPLY WITHOUT OWNER APPROVAL ***

The QCA6390 reports board_id 0xff, so ath11k loads the generic
"bus=pci,qmi-chip-id=0,qmi-board-id=255" entry of board-2.bin (QCA reference
design calibration: TX power tables, antenna gains, regulatory limits).
With this property the driver first asks for
"bus=pci,qmi-chip-id=0,qmi-board-id=255,variant=Lenovo_Q706F".

That entry is not in linux-firmware. scripts/desktop/setup-wifi-board.sh
builds a board-2.bin containing it from the stock bdwlan.elf (modem
partition, image/qca6390/; proprietary, never in the repo). Install that file
first: if the variant entry is missing the driver falls back to the generic
entry, so the patch alone is harmless but useless.

Unverified: nothing was tested with the stock board data yet (range, TX
power, default country). Keep the previous boot image at hand: a bad board
file means no Wi-Fi, and Wi-Fi may be the only way into the tablet.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-lenovo-q706f.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-lenovo-q706f.dts
@@ -1223,6 +1223,8 @@
 		vddrfa1p7-supply = <&vreg_pmu_rfa_1p7>;
 		vddpcie0p9-supply = <&vreg_pmu_pcie_0p9>;
 		vddpcie1p8-supply = <&vreg_pmu_pcie_1p8>;
+
+		qcom,calibration-variant = "Lenovo_Q706F";
 	};
 };
 
